These modules are written for TileLang (https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang), MIT License, Copyright (c) Tile-AI.
They are separate source files that run on an unmodified TileLang install; they do not modify
TileLang.

third_party/tilelang/ holds two unmodified TileLang files (examples/gemm_sm120/sm120_nvfp4_blockscaled_gemm.py,
maint/gemm/gemm_sm120/tilelang_nvfp4_quantizer.py) under TileLang's MIT License; see third_party/tilelang/LICENSE.

Several kernels reproduce the numerics or data formats of vLLM (Apache-2.0), FlashInfer (Apache-2.0), Marlin
(Apache-2.0), flash-linear-attention (MIT) and PyTorch Inductor/Triton (BSD-3-Clause / MIT) so that their
outputs are bit-identical. They are independent TileLang implementations; those projects are credited here
for the formats and algorithms they define.
